art:artigo_2203_00130v1_contribuicao_1 a art:Contribuicao ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "In summary, this paper contributes: (1) A characterization of the barriers readers face when they approach medical research papers."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_contribuicao_2 a art:Contribuicao ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 6 ;
    art:texto "(2) Paper Plain, an interactive reading interface for research papers that integrates existing affordances like term definition tooltips with novel affordances like in-situ plain language summaries of paper sections and a collection of key questions that guide readers to answering passages in the paper with paired plain language answers (§4)."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_contribuicao_3 a art:Contribuicao ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 6 ;
    art:texto "(3) Evidence from our usability study that these new affordances helped readers quickly find places in a paper that were informative to them."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_metodo_1 a art:Metodo ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "To improve access to medical papers, we introduce a novel interactive interface - Paper Plain1 - with four features powered by natural language processing: definitions of unfamiliar terms, in-situ plain language section summaries, a collection of key questions that guide readers to answering passages, and plain language summaries of the answering passages."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_metodo_2 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "To improve access to medical papers, we develop a novel interactive system, Paper Plain, through an iterative design process."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_metodo_3 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "The system is designed to make medical papers accessible with four features (illustrated in Figure 1) that combine to provide support at multiple levels of granularity (e.g., term, paragraph, section) and throughout the reading process."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_objetivo_1 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "In this paper, we ask how interactive information interfaces can make the research literature approachable to non-expert healthcare consumers that need it - whom we refer to as \"readers\" in this paper."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_objetivo_2 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_10 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "In this paper we ask how interactive interfaces can make medical research papers approachable to healthcare consumers that need it."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_problema_1 a art:Problema ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "Reading medical papers, however, can be a challenging experience."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_problema_2 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 6 ;
    art:texto "However, these resources do not cover all medical conditions and treatments [9, 90], especially those which are the focus of emerging research [17, 86]."@en .

