art:artigo_2203_00130v1_trabalho_futuro_1 a art:TrabalhoFuturo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_10 ;
    art:pontuacao 7 ;
    art:texto "We offer the following guidance for developing such future systems: Provide reading guidance Interactive reading systems for non-experts can provide more active support for guiding readers."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_trabalho_futuro_2 a art:TrabalhoFuturo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_10 ;
    art:pontuacao 7 ;
    art:texto "Future systems could go further by reporting factuality measures along with generated text [83] or integrating a feedback mechanism for reporting inconsistent information in order to crowd-source these factuality checks."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_trabalho_futuro_3 a art:TrabalhoFuturo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_10 ;
    art:pontuacao 7 ;
    art:texto "We are excited to integrate new advances for measuring and ensuring factuality in generations (e.g., [33, 60, 77]) into Paper Plain to help realize the promise of such models in real-world settings."@en .

art:artigo_2203_00130v1_trabalho_futuro_4 a art:TrabalhoFuturo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2203_00130v1_secao_10 ;
    art:pontuacao 13 ;
    art:texto "In future work we are excited to observe the use of Paper Plain in more naturalistic settings."@en .

art:artigo_2206_10883v3_contribuicao_1 a art:Contribuicao ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2206_10883v3_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "But to our knowledge, Multi-LexSum is the first dataset to provide summaries at multiple levels of granularity."@en .

art:artigo_2206_10883v3_metodo_1 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2206_10883v3_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "We conduct a series of experiments on Multi-LexSum, and find that existing summarization models perform poorly."@en .

art:artigo_2206_10883v3_objetivo_1 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2206_10883v3_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "We present extensive analysis demonstrating that despite the high-quality summaries in the training data (adhering to strict content and style guidelines), state-of-the-art summarization models perform poorly on this task."@en .

art:artigo_2206_10883v3_objetivo_2 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2206_10883v3_secao_2 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "In this paper, we present a new dataset, Multi-LexSum, for studying automatic summarization in an important real-world application setting found in the Civil Rights Litigation Clearinghouse (CRLC)."@en .

art:artigo_2206_10883v3_problema_1 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2206_10883v3_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "With the advent of large language models, methods for abstractive summarization have made great strides, creating potential for use in applications to aid knowledge workers processing unwieldy document collections."@en .

art:artigo_2206_10883v3_problema_2 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2206_10883v3_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "Multi-LexSum presents a challenging multi-document summarization task given the length of the source documents, often exceeding two hundred pages per case."@en .

