art:artigo_2304_02623v1_metodo_1 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2304_02623v1_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "We characterize expository writing as evidence-based and knowledge-generating: it contains summaries of external documents as well as new information or knowledge."@en .

art:artigo_2304_02623v1_metodo_2 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2304_02623v1_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "We sketch three components for AI support design and discuss considerations for future research."@en .

art:artigo_2304_02623v1_metodo_3 a art:Metodo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2304_02623v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 3 ;
    art:texto "For example, when starting writing a survey paper, the authors come up with the query to find relevant papers first, and AI helps execute the search and discover related documents; after authors read the retrieved papers and come up with ideas for the writing, AI can help generate the writing text based on authors' ideas, and the writers only need to proofread model output."@en .

art:artigo_2304_02623v1_objetivo_1 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2304_02623v1_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 5 ;
    art:texto "In this position paper, we argue that developing AI supports for expository writing has unique and exciting research challenges and can lead to high real-world impacts."@en .

art:artigo_2304_02623v1_objetivo_2 a art:Objetivo ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2304_02623v1_secao_6 ;
    art:pontuacao 4 ;
    art:texto "In this paper, we argue that the unique characteristics in expository writing open up new opportunities for designing AI support."@en .

art:artigo_2304_02623v1_problema_1 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2304_02623v1_secao_1 ;
    art:pontuacao 8 ;
    art:texto "However, AI-supported expository writing - including real-world tasks like scholars writing literature reviews or doctors writing progress notes - is relatively understudied."@en .

art:artigo_2304_02623v1_problema_2 a art:Problema ;
    art:extraidoDe art:artigo_2304_02623v1_secao_3 ;
    art:pontuacao 8 ;
    art:texto "While prior work has explored many exciting applications for LLMs, we argue thatexpository writing is a task that is understudied in existing work on AI augmented writing."@en .

